# pi loads EVERY .md at the root of a configured skills directory as a skill
# (loadSkillsFromDirInternal with includeRootFiles), so this directory's own
# README.md was parsed as one and reported at every start:
#
#   [Skill conflicts]
#     ~/repos/hive-pi__worktrees/main/skills/README.md
#       description is required
#
# pi honours .gitignore / .ignore / .fdignore here, and .ignore is the right one:
# the README must stay tracked in git, it just is not a skill. Subdirectories are
# unaffected — a directory containing SKILL.md is a skill root and is not
# recursed into, which is why craft-ui/references/*.md never had this problem.
README.md
